  "snp3.5:1.3": "Māgha (“bounteous one”) is from the Vedic word <i lang='pi' translate='no'>magha</i>, “gift, bounty”. It is a name of Sakka (<a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn2.3/en/sujato'>SN 2.3</a>), as is the synonymous Maghavā (<a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn11.12/en/sujato#1.3'>SN 11.12:1.3</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn11.13/en/sujato#6.1'>SN 11.13:6.1</a>). The good king of <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn83/en/sujato'>MN 83</a> is named Maghadeva, “god of bounty”. ",
