  "snp3.5:24.1": "The “speaker’s mark” is in MS treated as part of the line, which is unusual. According to Norman’s note here however, we should consider this line a seven-syllable sloka (perhaps restoring the variant <i lang='pi' translate='no'>ca</i> to make it eight). I have adjusted the Pali punctuation accordingly. ",
